# Additional Permission — Plugin Builds

This section is granted by the licensor **in addition to** the Terms and
Conditions above. It only adds permission; it takes nothing away.

Project Indexer has no runtime plugin loader, by design — native code loaded
into the process cannot be sandboxed. Using a plugin therefore means building
the Software with that plugin included. Without the permission below,
distributing such a build would be a Competing Use, and a plugin author could
not hand anyone a working copy of their own work.

## What this covers

A **Plugin Build** is a copy of the Software that differs from a release we
publish only by the addition of one or more plugins: configuration consumed by
the Software's theming and layout mechanisms, or code registered through its
documented extension points.

A copy that removes, replaces or reimplements functionality of the Software is
not a Plugin Build, and nothing in this section applies to it.

## The permission

Distributing a Plugin Build, in source or binary form, is a Permitted Purpose
and is not a Competing Use, provided that:

1. it is not presented as an official release, and is named and described so
   that it will not be mistaken for one;
2. it carries these Terms and Conditions, including this section, together with
   the copyright notices already present in the Software; and
3. it states which release it is built from and which plugins were added.

## What this does not do

This permission covers distributing the Plugin Build. It does not license the
plugins themselves. A plugin is its author's own work, carries whatever licence
its author chooses, and is not made subject to these Terms and Conditions by
being built into a Plugin Build.
